{
  "name": "Monthly roll of Sitara transport usage tickets",
  "today": "Before each new month Heidi Withers (rates group) goes through the HPL and third-party transport usage tickets in Sitara one by one, adds the new month where needed and refreshes each rate by hand to match the rate matrix. When she adds a month she leaves the volume at zero, so the schedulers on Daren Farmer's desk must fill in volumes and are told to check every pipe. The correct rates already sit in Unify for invoicing, so the Sitara tickets are a second, hand-kept copy, and mismatches with the matrix have been found.",
  "change": "A month-end job extends each active usage ticket, fills its rate from the matrix/Unify rates and carries last month's volume, leaving people only an exception list.",
  "explanation": "A scheduled job run before month start extends each active transport usage ticket by one month (or copies it to a new ticket where a ticket's term is full). It sets the rate from the same rate table in Unify that invoicing uses, and sets the volume to the prior month's figure instead of zero. It then lists only the tickets it could not price: new baseload deals and third-party paths whose rates are not yet known. Heidi or the desk fills in those, as they already must today. Schedulers change volumes only where flows actually change. The ticket-rate check that Heidi now does by Basis Adjustment report becomes an automatic comparison of ticket rate against matrix rate.",
  "occurrences": [
    {
      "file": "corpus/farmer-d/logistics/1144.eml",
      "quote": "I updated the June transport usage tickets today through HPL, and will be \nfinishing these tickets tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/farmer-d/logistics/1257.eml",
      "quote": "I have input and updated transport usage tickets for July."
    }
  ],
  "evidence": [
    {
      "file": "corpus/farmer-d/logistics/1144.eml",
      "quote": "Rates have been updated to reflect current \nmatrix rates and all baseload rates that I know of at this time.",
      "note": "Rates are refreshed by hand against the matrix on every ticket; the job would fill these automatically."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/farmer-d/logistics/1144.eml",
      "quote": "Rule of thumb \nwas that if I had to add a month, I refreshed the rate but left volume at \nzero.",
      "note": "Added months start at zero volume, which creates re-entry work for the schedulers."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/farmer-d/logistics/1144.eml",
      "quote": "I would advise that your schedulers check volumes on all pipes to ensure \nthey're reflected in Position Manager correctly.",
      "note": "The desk's schedulers are drawn into checking every pipe after the roll."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/farmer-d/logistics/1145.eml",
      "quote": "The tickets are finished.",
      "note": "Sent the next morning: the roll ran from the afternoon of 24 May into the morning of 25 May, roughly a working day of Heidi's time."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/farmer-d/logistics/867.eml",
      "quote": "The rates are in the system correctly in Unify (so that we can invoice \ncorrectly), but Daren's group uses a Sitara deal (the transport usage \ntickets) to estimate desk transport in the P&L during the month.",
      "note": "The correct rates already exist in a system, so the Sitara rates are a duplicate copy that could be filled from it."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/farmer-d/logistics/867.eml",
      "quote": "Lauri's matrix shows 0.05 from Thompsonville \nto HSC, but the transport usage ticket (updated by Daren's group) has 0.055.",
      "note": "Hand-kept ticket rates drift from the matrix."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/farmer-d/logistics/1257.eml",
      "quote": "I do not yet know what baseload rates you have agreed upon, so you \nwill need to adjust them in the appropriate tickets.",
      "note": "Baseload and third-party rates are not in the matrix; these stay manual and are the exception list."
    }
  ],
  "stalls": [],
  "ongoing": true,
  "stated_rate": null,
  "minutes": 280
}

