{
  "name": "Pulling gas P&L top pages and curve-shift reports for Arthur Andersen's monthly testing",
  "today": "Each month Arthur Andersen (Sharon Smith, Carrie Richardson, Mark Austin) picks gas books or regions from the monthly Natural Gas P&L. They email the Houston gas risk controllers (Giron, Keiser, Kelly, Baumbach, and later others) for the P&L top page for the last day of the month. Where most of a book's P&L comes from curve shift, they also want the top pages and curve-shift reports for the five largest days. Each controller forwards the request to their book administrators, who find, print and copy the reports. AA then chases items still missing, sometimes months later, to close a quarter file. The reports already exist, because they come out of the nightly P&L.",
  "change": "Save every book's daily P&L top page and curve-shift report from the nightly P&L run to a dated, read-only folder that the auditors can open, so AA picks its monthly samples itself.",
