{
  "name": "Nightly check that every gas book and post ID is official",
  "today": "Every book and post ID on the gas risk desks must be marked official each night, or V@R and credit pick up wrong positions. Michael Moscoso's group tracks books that were not made official every day, and that list goes to Sally Beck and is reviewed weekly by Rick Buy. After the West desk missed a book in October 2000, the desks were told to put a control in place. Dutch Quigley sent the five regional leads an Excel macro that, once someone types in the date, portfolio and book codes, queries which books are official. On Darron Giron's West desk the last person finished each night must run it, and regional controllers get an end-of-night sheet confirming all books are official. The existing benchmark sign-off does not catch a post ID that has no net position, which is how the West miss got through.",
  "change": "The risk system checks after the nightly calc which calculated books and post IDs are not official, including flat ones, and alerts each book's owner by name, so nobody has to run the macro by hand.",
  "explanation": "A scheduled query in the risk system runs after the nightly calc window. It lists every book and post ID that calculated that day but is not marked official, whether or not it has a net position. It sends the list straight to that book's administrator and regional lead, and escalates if a book is still open at a cut-off time. The same output becomes the end-of-night sheet for regional controllers and the daily list for Moscoso's Beck/Buy report. Afterwards no desk runs the macro or keys in portfolio and book codes. People act only when a book is flagged, and the gap for flat post IDs is closed.",
  "occurrences": [
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/533.eml",
      "quote": "I think Jason has been \nrunning the official post id macro most nights, but we need to have the last \nperson finished do it every day."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/582.eml",
      "quote": "Use it to make sure all your postid's that need to be, are \nofficialized each night."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/595.eml",
      "quote": "We have been tracking books that are not officialized on a daily basis."
    }
  ],
  "evidence": [
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/582.eml",
      "quote": "To run this file all that has to be done is enter the date and have the \nPortfolio and Book CD entered in also.",
      "note": "The nightly check is done by hand: someone enters the date and codes, runs the query and reads the result. The scheduled query removes this."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/582.eml",
      "quote": "To: Jeffrey C Gossett/HOU/ECT@ECT, David Baumbach/HOU/ECT@ECT, William \nKelly/HOU/ECT@ECT, Darron C Giron/HOU/ECT@ECT, Kam Keiser/HOU/ECT@ECT",
      "note": "The macro went to all the regional leads, so each region's desk is expected to run it, not only the West."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/533.eml",
      "quote": "2. All regional controllers will receive a sheet at the end of the night, \nverifying that all books are officialized.",
      "note": "A nightly verification sheet is produced for the controllers; the system output would replace it."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/595.eml",
      "quote": "This \nlist goes to Sally Beck and is reviewed at the end of each week by Rick Buy.",
      "note": "A separate daily list of books not made official is kept for senior management; the system output would feed it."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/595.eml",
      "quote": "If a postid has a net position and is not \nofficialized, it will be caught using this procedure.  It will not, however, \nif the postid does not have a position.",
      "note": "The existing check misses flat post IDs; checking official status directly closes that gap."
    },
    {
